• TEST CONDITIONS:-
1. Implement a polynomial representation using a circular linked list
• Create a polynomial with multiple terms entered in sequence
• Create a Polynomial with a single term
• Create an empty polynomial with 0 terms
• Verify that the last node points back to the first node
2. Perform polynomial operations (Create, Display, Addition)
• Display a polynomial with multiple terms.
• Add two polynomials having common exponents.
• Add two polynomials having no common exponents
• Add polynomials with negative coefficients
3. Understand efficient handling of polynomial arithmetic using Circular linked list
• Perform repeated traversal of the polynomial
• Verify memory allocation for dynamic node creation.
• Display the resultant polynomial after addition
 
